{{/*
family: web-ui
what: syslog
transports: udp, tcp, tls
reference: RFC 5424 (severities, facilities), RFC 5426 (UDP), RFC 6587 (TCP), RFC 5425 (TLS)
verification: reference
*/}}
{{define "does"}}The values to enter in the device's syslog (remote logging) page so it sends {{.Severity.Word}} and more severe messages to Woodshed over {{if eq .Transport "udp"}}UDP{{else if eq .Transport "tcp"}}TCP{{else}}TLS{{end}}.{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part steps - In the device's web page, open its syslog or remote logging settings and enter
Remote logging: on
Server address: {{.Address}}
Port: {{.Port}}
Protocol: {{if eq .Transport "udp"}}UDP{{else if eq .Transport "tcp"}}TCP{{else}}TLS (sometimes called secure or encrypted syslog){{end}}
{{- if eq .Transport "tls"}}
CA certificate: Woodshed's, from Settings → TLS → CA certificate (PEM to paste, DER to upload)
Server name to check: {{.TLSName}}{{end}}
Lowest severity to send: {{.Severity.Word}} ({{.Severity.Num}})
Facility: {{if .Facility}}{{.Facility}}{{else}}leave the device's default{{end}}
Message format: RFC 5424 if offered, otherwise the default
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
Field names differ between devices; some put the port into the address field as {{.HostPort}}.
{{- if eq .Transport "tls"}}
{{if .CASHA256}}Compare the CA fingerprint the device shows with {{.CASHA256}}. {{end}}If the device checks the server's name, use {{.TLSName}}{{if not .TLSNameKnown}} (it must be a DNS name on Woodshed's certificate; Settings → TLS lists them once TLS is on){{end}}; many check names only, not IP addresses.
{{- end}}
Pages that offer a "send a test message" button usually send it at once: watch the Dashboard.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}The device appears on Woodshed's Dashboard with its first message, often right after you save.{{end}}
